.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_ENTER 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_enter ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_leave
.Nd move a stream across a scope boundary
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_enter "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_scope *child"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_leave "dtfl_stream *st"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_enter
projects
.Fa st ,
a stream of some scope, into
.Fa child ,
a direct child of that scope, and returns the matching stream in the
child.
Each record keeps its data; its time is refined to the child's class by
.Fn Refines::to_inner :
for a region the time is unchanged, for an iterative
.Pq product
scope it gains the minimum inner coordinate, and for an alternating
scope it is doubled.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_leave
projects
.Fa st ,
a stream of a child scope, back into that scope's parent, and returns
the stream in the parent.
Each time is projected by
.Fn to_outer ,
the inverse of
.Fn to_inner :
a region time is unchanged, an iterative scope drops its inner
coordinate, and an alternating time is halved.
.Pp
Both are checked at build time:
.Fn dtfl_stream_enter
panics unless
.Fa child
is a direct child of the stream's scope, and
.Fn dtfl_stream_leave
panics unless the stream's scope has a parent.
Neither adds a scheduled operator; the projection is a pusher wired
directly onto the scope boundary, so a pass-through region costs
nothing at run time.
Progress crosses the boundary correctly because the boundary edge is
recorded for the progress tracker.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each returns the projected stream, owned by the destination scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_scope_region(scope, "region", build_region, &ctx);

static void build_region(dtfl_scope *inner, void *arg) {
	struct ctx *c = arg;
	dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_stream_enter(c->data, inner);
	s = dtfl_stream_filter(s, keep, DTFL_NOCTX);
	c->result = dtfl_stream_leave(s);
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
A scope that is not the required parent or child is a programming error
and calls the panic hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_scope_scoped 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn enter
and
.Fn leave
operators of
.Pa core/enterleave.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Both streams and the boundary pusher belong to the worker thread that
built them.
The projection runs on that thread during the worker's steps.
